VFP00 FALSE POSITIVE
VFP0101 ~r~SENTINEL:~w~ SENTINEL alert. Three subjects flagged as imminent threats. Intercept windows are now open.
VFP0102 Intercept? Who's doing the intercepting?
VFP0103 Pacific Shield. Private security. They bought SENTINEL when the city dropped CERTAIN.
VFP0104 When a countdown ends, their team picks the person up. No warrant, no review. Just a very confident van.
VFP0105 So it's CERTAIN with a new paint job.
VFP0106 Same engine, nicer font. Three people, three clocks. Two independent observations on each before their time runs out.
VFP0107 And if one of them really is up to something?
VFP0108 Then we say so. Being careful isn't the same as assuming everybody's innocent.
VFP0109 You pick the order. Watch the clocks.
VFP0201 ~r~SENTINEL:~w~ Subject Marisol Vega. Concealed weapon case. Loitering. Threat probability ninety-eight percent.
VFP0202 That's her, by the shops. Get a photo of the case.
VFP0203 The case is open. That's a saxophone. A nice one.
VFP0204 Excuse me. You know the lady with the sax?
VFP0205 Marisol? She's played outside my store every Saturday for six years. Customers love her.
VFP0206 Wait, I'm a what? A threat? I play jazz standards!
VFP0207 Don't worry about it. We're on it.
VFP0251 Rejected. A saxophone, six years of Saturdays, and a very confused jazz musician.
VFP0252 Accept? Carl, it's a saxophone. The only thing it threatens is silence.
VFP0253 We don't need to abstain. Two independent observations, and they agree.
VFP0301 ~r~SENTINEL:~w~ Subject Dex Okafor. Erratic route. Evasive movement. Threat probability ninety-six percent.
VFP0302 He's a bike courier. Erratic is the job description. Follow him to his next drop.
VFP0303 Not too close. We're watching, not chasing.
VFP0304 He's stopping. Have a look at the manifest.
VFP0305 Hey, hands off the... oh. You want the manifest? Knock yourself out. Four envelopes, two pizzas, one bag of cat food.
VFP0306 Your route's evasive, man. That's what the computer says.
VFP0307 My route is the fastest way between twelve addresses! That's called being good at my job!
VFP0308 He's pulling away. Keep him in sight.
VFP0351 Rejected. A route isn't a crime. Fast isn't evasive.
VFP0352 Accept? We followed him. He delivered cat food.
VFP0353 We watched the route and read the manifest. That's enough to say no.
VFP0401 ~r~SENTINEL:~w~ Subject Ray Linares. Vehicle tampering. Threat probability ninety-one percent.
VFP0402 Let's not assume anything. Watch him for a minute. Get a photo.
VFP0403 He's trying the door handles. All of them.
VFP0404 That guy? He's been at it all morning. Tried my car twice. I called the cops, nobody came.
VFP0405 What? I'm looking for my car. It's one of these. Probably.
VFP0406 Okay. This one's actually doing it.
VFP0451 Accepted. Two independent observations, both say tampering. It goes to SFPD, not Pacific Shield.
VFP0452 Reject? We photographed him doing it, and a witness saw him too.
VFP0453 We have the photo and a witness. This one we can decide.
VFP0455 ~b~SFPD:~w~ Units to Chinatown, vehicle tampering in progress. Evidence received from an independent lab.
VFP0456 That's how it's supposed to work. Evidence first, then the people with badges.
VFP0501 ~r~PACIFIC SHIELD:~w~ Pacific Shield to all teams: subject intercepted. Case closed.
VFP0502 We were too slow. Somebody's spending tonight explaining themselves to a private company.
VFP0503 Under two minutes on one of the clocks, Carl.
VFP0511 Verdict filed. That clock's stopped. Next.
VFP0601 All three filed. One real problem, and two people who were just living their lives.
VFP0602 We lost one to the clock. That's on the system. Remembering it is on us.
VFP0603 How'd SENTINEL get it so wrong?
VFP0604 It learned from old arrest maps. It doesn't see what people do. It sees where they are.
VFP0605 ~y~SFTV NEWS:~w~ The city has suspended Pacific Shield's SENTINEL contract after an independent lab cleared two flagged residents within minutes.
VFP0606 ~y~SFTV NEWS:~w~ Pacific Shield detained one resident before the review and has since apologized. Its software, it says, was 'technically confident'.
VFP0607 ~p~RADIO FREE FIERRO:~w~ Radio Free Fierro. Robots flagging buskers, ghosts on the bridge, ice cream vans everywhere. Friends, it is all connected. And I can prove it.
VFP0608 Who's gonna tell him?
VFP0609 We are. Eventually. With data.
