VGF00 GHOST FREQUENCY
VGF0101 ~p~RADIO FREE FIERRO:~w~ Radio Free Fierro, you're on the air. Tell me about the beeping.
VGF0102 ~p~CALLER:~w~ It's in my clock radio, Rex. Seven little beeps and a long one. Every night. My dog won't go in the kitchen.
VGF0103 ~p~RADIO FREE FIERRO:~w~ Friends, that is not interference. That is a message. San Fierro has a ghost, and it's trying to talk.
VGF0104 Your radio's haunted, man.
VGF0105 Listen.
VGF0106 Seven short, one long, every ninety seconds, on one-six-six megahertz. People hear it all over the city.
VGF0107 So it's a ghost with a schedule.
VGF0108 Ghosts don't keep schedules. Transmitters do. A real ghost would have a favourite haunt. Let's find this one's.
VGF0109 We take bearings from two places. Where the lines cross, that's where it lives. Roughly.
VGF0110 Roughly?
VGF0111 Roughly is the honest version of exactly.
VGF0201 The receiver turns the signal into a needle and a sound. Watch the needle, but trust your ears.
VGF0202 Why my ears?
VGF0203 Because noise is loud and the pattern is quiet. Loud things like to pretend they're important.
VGF0204 Sounds like half the people I know.
VGF0205 ~p~RADIO FREE FIERRO:~w~ Callers say the beeping is loudest near Queens. Coincidence? I don't believe in coincidences. I believe in Queens.
VGF0221 Park on the marker and hold still. The antenna does the rest.
VGF0222 Bearing one. Strong, too.
VGF0223 Bearing two. The lines cross in Queens. Near a nightclub.
VGF0224 Hold still. You're smearing the bearing.
VGF0241 The needle's pinned here. But listen to it.
VGF0242 That's just buzzing.
VGF0243 That sign has a dying transformer. It sprays noise into every channel, ours included.
VGF0244 R.A.I.N. wants a verdict. Is this our ghost?
VGF0261 Rejected. Loud isn't the same as the source. The pattern's still out there, under the buzz.
VGF0262 Accept? Carl, it's buzzing. Our ghost beeps. Listen again.
VGF0263 We can do better than abstain. The pattern isn't in this noise at all. That's a reject.
VGF0264 So we followed the loudest thing in the city.
VGF0265 Everybody does. That's why it's a trap. New plan: on foot, with the handheld, away from the sign.
VGF0301 Take the handheld. Turn slowly. When the beeps get clean and loud, hold it there.
VGF0302 That's a bearing. Back in the van.
VGF0303 Wait. This one points straight up at the bridge.
VGF0304 So the ghost lives on the Gant Bridge. Rex was right?
VGF0305 Or the bridge is a mirror. The cables bounce the signal. We might be hearing an echo.
VGF0306 Same question for R.A.I.N. Is the source on the bridge?
VGF0321 Rejected. The bearing swings when we move. A real source holds still. An echo doesn't.
VGF0322 If it was up there, the bearing wouldn't move when we did. It moved. Try again.
VGF0323 We have the swing on record. That's evidence. It's an echo, so we can reject this.
VGF0324 One more bearing from the Esplanade, away from the cables. Then we cross the lines properly.
VGF0325 There. Three clean bearings, one crossing. Downtown, by the parking structure.
VGF0401 That's a SureThing van. And that's a relay dish going into the back of it.
VGF0402 Oh, come on. I'm on my lunch.
VGF0403 He's leaving! If the relay goes with him, so does our evidence.
VGF0404 Stop the van. Don't hurt him. We need him talking.
VGF0405 Okay! Okay! I'm out! I just install the things, man!
VGF0406 Install what?
VGF0407 Relays. Upload boxes. They told me CERTAIN was switched off. They said these were for weather.
VGF0408 Weather with a CERTAIN header on every packet.
VGF0409 Look, I don't get paid enough to have an opinion.
VGF0410 Grab the relay out of the back, Carl.
VGF0451 So. We could publish the recording right now. Everybody's listening. The timing's perfect.
VGF0452 Or we take the relay to the lab and check it properly. But it's wiping its own memory. We'd have four minutes.
VGF0453 And if we put it out now?
VGF0454 Then SureThing says we faked a beep, and they'll pick at every gap. Your call, Carl.
VGF0471 Shielded box in the lab. Four minutes. Drive the way you always drive, but on purpose.
VGF0472 Two minutes. The memory counter's falling.
VGF0473 We're here. Box, now!
VGF0474 Wiped. We've still got the recording. It just won't carry the same weight.
VGF0481 Uploading the recording to the registry. Done. Now it's everybody's ghost.
VGF0482 Let's take the relay back anyway. No rush.
VGF0501 Control run. Relay unplugged... silence. Plugged in... seven short, one long. It's the relay.
VGF0502 And every packet says STC-CERT. CERTAIN was supposed to be switched off two weeks ago.
VGF0503 So the ghost was a robot that didn't know it got fired.
VGF0504 That is honestly the best summary I've heard.
VGF0505 ~y~SFTV NEWS:~w~ SureThing Technologies confirms a 'legacy relay' was left running in Downtown San Fierro. The company says it was a clerical error.
VGF0506 ~y~SFTV NEWS:~w~ SureThing calls a recording released by an independent lab 'unverifiable'. The lab has published its methods and invited anyone to check them.
VGF0507 ~p~RADIO FREE FIERRO:~w~ So it was a robot. Fine. But who's to say a robot can't be a ghost? Lines are open.
VGF0508 Man, this city.
