VHN01 SF GAZETTE: Independent Doherty lab keeps its findings public. 'Check our work,' says founder.
VHQ0101 Carl. Welcome to Vers3Dynamics. Officially, this time.
VHQ0102 Officially? What, you got a sign now?
VHQ0103 I've got a doormat. It's a start.
VHQ0104 R.A.I.N.'s got research assignments queued up. Small stuff. Good practice for the big stuff.
VHQ0105 Use whatever you like. The plate, the terminal, the diagrams. Just not the red cable.
VHQ0106 What's the red cable do?
VHQ0107 That's what I'd like to know.
VHQ0111 Carl. Pull up a chair. Not that one, it's load-bearing.
VHQ0112 Back again? The coffee's terrible, but the data's good.
VHQ0113 You're just in time. I was about to start arguing with myself.
VHQ0114 Welcome back. Mind the cables. And the other cables.
VHQ0115 We're in the paper again, Carl. Not the good page.
VHQ0116 Good news: the paper liked our last result. I've framed it. Mentally.
VHQ0117 The registry's had forty thousand visitors. Forty thousand and one, counting my mother.
VHQ0201 So what do you actually do all day?
VHQ0202 Mostly I try to prove myself wrong. It's going great.
VHQ0203 Why'd you call the computer R.A.I.N.?
VHQ0204 Recursive Architecture for Intelligent Nexus. Every layer checks the layer underneath.
VHQ0205 And it spells rain. That's a coincidence?
VHQ0206 Absolutely not. I'm not a monster.
VHQ0207 You ever sleep, man?
VHQ0208 I run a sleep experiment every night. The results are mixed.
VHQ0209 That metal plate with the sand. What's that for?
VHQ0210 Cymatics. Sound you can see. Every pattern is the fingerprint of a frequency.
VHQ0211 Looks like somebody spilled sugar on a speaker.
VHQ0212 That is exactly what it is, actually.
VHQ0213 You still hearing that ghost beeping?
VHQ0214 Every time I close my eyes. Seven short, one long.
VHQ0215 Those people Sentinel flagged. They alright?
VHQ0216 They're suing. Politely. With our data.
VHQ0217 Man, I can't stop seeing patterns everywhere now.
VHQ0218 Good. Now ask which ones survive a second look.
VHQ0219 You could've been rich, you know.
VHQ0220 I am rich. I've got a garage full of cables and a friend who drives like a lunatic.
VHQ0221 Nice watch, Carl. New?
VHQ0222 ...It was on sale.
VHQ0223 How's my reputation looking?
VHQ0224 Ours. And it's only as good as our last careful answer.
VHQ0301 The whole city hums at sixty hertz. Somewhere between a B-flat and a bad mood.
VHQ0302 If this works I'll be very surprised. That's how you know it's an experiment.
VHQ0303 Note to self: label the cables. Note to self: you said that last week.
VHQ0304 Calibration's drifting. Either that or I am.
VHQ0305 Three independent readings. Not one reading three times.
VHQ0306 Hm. Interesting. No. Wait. Yes. Interesting.
VHQ0307 If you see smoke, that's normal. If you see flames, that's science.
VHQ0308 A correlation is a rumour. A cause needs a witness.
VHQ0309 The most dangerous number in the world is a confident one.
VHQ0310 Who keeps moving my oscilloscope? Oh. Me.
VHQ0401 R.A.I.N.'s all yours. Be nice to it. It remembers.
VHQ0402 Signal generator, steel plate, a pinch of sand. Find the frequencies where the plate rings.
VHQ0403 Careful: the building hums too. Switch the generator off and see what's still there.
VHQ0404 There it is. Look at that.
VHQ0405 Another one. The plate's singing now.
VHQ0406 That's a beauty. Write it down.
VHQ0407 Check it with the generator off. Still there? Then it's the wiring, not the plate.
VHQ0408 So the building was lying to me.
VHQ0409 Buildings do that. Now we know its voice.
VHQ0410 Six modes. A complete atlas. Carl, that's publishable.
VHQ0411 Do I get my name on it?
VHQ0412 Second author. Right behind the sand.
VHQ0413 Every result we've got. The good, the bad, and the burger.
VHQ0414 That's R.A.I.N.'s architecture. Every layer checks the one below it.
VHQ0415 CERTAIN's confidence against reality. Notice the two lines never touch.
VHQ0416 The plate modes. Physics doesn't care what anybody believes.
VHQ0417 Every red dot is a prediction. Every blue one is something we actually checked.
VHQ0501 Carl. Something's come up. Meet me by the desk when you're ready.
VHQ0502 There's a signal on the scanner nobody can explain. I'd like to explain it.
VHQ0503 Somebody leaked me a SENTINEL dashboard. It's flagging people. Right now.
VHQ0504 A radio host says everything in San Fierro is connected. I'd like to check his work.
VHQ0505 We're going public. Properly. Everything open, everything checkable.
VHQ0506 Drive safe. Or at least drive measurably.
VHQ0507 See you, Carl.
VHQ0508 Back to the field, then.
VHQ1011 Burger Shot says Tuesday Doubles make you lucky. I say: show me the losers.
VHQ1012 Rejected, cleanly. One caller quoted twice is still one caller.
VHQ1013 Right answer. But you counted the same caller twice. Luck isn't a method.
VHQ1014 We just told the city burgers cause luck. Burger Shot is on line one. They're delighted.
VHQ1015 We had the survey and it said no. Abstaining here is just being shy.
VHQ1016 Twenty-four winners, twenty-six losers. Same as any day.
VHQ1017 I ate the Double. I lost twenty bucks. And I feel terrible.
VHQ1021 Garcia says the new tower wrecks their TV. The timing matches. Timing matches a lot of things.
VHQ1022 Rejected. The tower was off and the static came anyway. It's the hair dryer.
VHQ1023 Right call, but a petition is a list of opinions, not observations.
VHQ1024 We blamed the tower. SureThing's lawyers have written to us. In crayon, but still.
VHQ1025 We switched the neighbour off and the picture came back. That's about as clear as it gets.
VHQ1026 Neighbour unplugs at six, picture's perfect. Old man cried a little.
VHQ1027 Sunny day, static anyway. Weather's off the hook.
VHQ1031 CERTAIN said ninety-nine point nine percent. Let's see how often ninety-nine point nine was right.
VHQ1032 Accepted. Overconfident everywhere, and two independent audits agree.
VHQ1033 Right, but that TV special was just our own log on the news. Same data, new haircut.
VHQ1034 We just vouched for CERTAIN. Max Certainty sent a fruit basket. I'm not eating it.
VHQ1035 Two separate audits, same answer. We're allowed to say it out loud.
VHQ1036 Wrong in every district. Even the fancy ones.
VHQ1037 They said, quote, CERTAIN is certain. Then they hung up on me.
VHQ1041 The Gant Bridge hums on windy nights. Rex Pattern says ghost. I say physics. One of us is annoying.
VHQ1042 Accepted. The wind plays the cables like a string. The bridge is just singing.
VHQ1043 Right answer, but one fisherman's bad night isn't data about a bridge.
VHQ1044 We just published that the bridge is haunted. Rex Pattern is thrilled. I need a lie down.
VHQ1045 The pitch follows the wind. That's a fingerprint. We can say this one.
VHQ1046 Wind goes up, hum goes up. Like blowing across a bottle.
VHQ1047 Cars come, cars go. The hum don't care.
VHQ1051 Ice cream and crime go up together. Either ice cream is a gateway dessert, or something else is going on.
VHQ1052 Rejected. Hot weather drives both. Ice cream is innocent.
VHQ1053 Right, but the union statement wasn't evidence. They'd defend ice cream if it bit people.
VHQ1054 We published that ice cream causes crime. There are ice cream vans outside. Several. Idling.
VHQ1055 The strike week told us. No vans, same crime. That's our answer.
VHQ1056 Hot days, crime goes up. Vans or no vans.
VHQ1057 I ate the cone. Nobody robbed nobody. Science.
VHQ1061 If we say this was CERTAIN, SureThing will check every byte. So let's check them first.
VHQ1062 Accepted. Header, schedule, a second receiver and a control. That's airtight.
VHQ1063 Right call, but Rex decoded BEWARE, then LUNCH. Leave him out of it.
VHQ1064 We said it was a ham-radio beacon. The ham-radio club is very confused.
VHQ1065 Unplug the relay and the bursts stop. We know where they come from.
VHQ1066 Relay unplugged, silence. Plug it back in, beep beep.
VHQ1067 Rex says it spells LUNCH now. Man's hungry.
VHQ1071 SENTINEL flags Ganton nine times more than Downtown, for the same behaviour. Let's test that properly.
VHQ1072 Accepted. It learned old arrest maps, not behaviour. Same walk, different street, different verdict.
VHQ1073 Right, but the vans follow the flags, not the other way round. Watch the arrows.
VHQ1074 We cleared SENTINEL. Pacific Shield put our quote on a billboard. Next to a lion.
VHQ1075 Two identical walkers, seven flags against none. We can stand behind this.
VHQ1076 Same dude, same walk. Ganton, flagged seven times. Downtown, nothing.
VHQ1077 They said proprietary. That's corporate for don't look.
VHQ1081 One reading under Mount Chiliad. One. I want it to be something, and that's exactly why I don't trust it.
VHQ1082 Abstained. One echo and a drifting array isn't a chamber. It isn't nothing either. We go back.
VHQ1083 Right to wait, but the hiker's lights aren't our echo. Different mystery.
VHQ1084 We picked an answer the data can't carry. Either way, somebody's heading up Chiliad with a shovel.
VHQ1085 Sometimes the bravest thing to say is: not yet.
VHQ1086 Steady temperature, echo's weaker. Still something. Maybe.
VHQ1087 I climbed up there. Found a rock. And a goat. Goat ain't talking.
