VOE00 THE OPEN EXPERIMENT
VOE0101 Tomorrow we run the plate experiment in public. Everything open: the method, the data, the mistakes.
VOE0102 And three independent groups run the same experiment at the same time, across town. If they get our result, it's real.
VOE0103 And if they don't?
VOE0104 Then we were wrong in front of everybody, and we learn something. Win-win.
VOE0105 Gentlemen! Lyle Bracket, Ovid Venture Partners. The door was open. I love an open door.
VOE0106 Two hundred and fifty thousand dollars for an exclusive licence on R.A.I.N. We close the code, we polish the brand, everybody gets rich.
VOE0107 That's generous. And no.
VOE0108 Closed systems sell, Mister Woodyard. Open ones get copied. The offer stands. For your friend, too.
VOE0109 He seems nice.
VOE0110 He seems like a man who's never been told no by a garage. Let's get the kits out.
VOE0201 Three replication kits: a plate, a generator, a pinch of sand, and instructions a teenager can follow.
VOE0202 One to the physics teacher at Garcia High, one to the ham radio club in Ocean Flats, one to the kid who won the science fair.
VOE0211 Real equipment? For my class? Oh, they are going to lose their minds.
VOE0212 Four forty-two hertz, tomorrow at noon. Write down whatever you see.
VOE0213 Even if it's nothing?
VOE0214 Especially if it's nothing. That's what he says.
VOE0221 A Chladni plate. We'll calibrate the generator against our frequency standard. To the hertz.
VOE0222 Man, you're gonna be good at this.
VOE0231 If your result doesn't replicate, I'm putting that in my report.
VOE0232 Kid, that's exactly what he wants.
VOE0241 Black sedan, three cars back. It's been there since Garcia.
VOE0242 Ovid's people. If they rattle the van hard enough, the kits crack. Lose them.
VOE0243 That knock broke a kit. One group fewer.
VOE0244 They've dropped off. Good driving.
VOE0301 The pier. Look at all these people. Some of them even came on purpose.
VOE0302 Deputy Commissioner Halvorsen, procurement. This event has no permit for experimental equipment. Shut it down.
VOE0303 It's a speaker and a metal plate, Commissioner. The schematics are on the registry. You're welcome to check them.
VOE0304 I am not here to check things. I am here to stop things.
VOE0305 Lady, that's the whole problem with this city.
VOE0306 The generator's dead. Somebody pulled the fuse. There! The guy in the overalls!
VOE0307 Carl, get that fuse back. Don't hurt him.
VOE0308 Give it here, man! Now!
VOE0309 Fuse is in. We're live.
VOE0310 He got away. We'll run it off the van battery. It'll be quieter, but it'll work.
VOE0401 Four hundred and forty-two hertz. Watch the sand.
VOE0402 ~y~CROWD:~w~ Whoa! It's making a pattern!
VOE0403 Garcia High here! Same pattern! Crosses and curves, exactly like your picture!
VOE0404 Ocean Flats Amateur Radio Club. Mode confirmed at four forty-two, plus or minus one.
VOE0405 It worked. I hate that it worked. It's in my report.
VOE0406 R.A.I.N.'s question for all of us: does the result hold up?
VOE0411 Accepted. Independent groups, independent equipment, same result. That's what real looks like.
VOE0412 Reject it? Carl, they all got the pattern. On their own kit.
VOE0413 We don't need to abstain. More than one independent replication. We can say it.
VOE0414 Abstained. One replication is a promising start, not a confirmation. We publish it as exactly that.
VOE0415 Accept, on one replication? I'd love to. That's exactly why we shouldn't.
VOE0416 Reject? One group confirmed it. That's not nothing. It's not enough, either.
VOE0417 ...The city will be reviewing its permit process.
VOE0501 Carl. A word. Your friend won't sell. But friends can be persuaded.
VOE0502 Fifty thousand dollars. Cash. All you have to do is talk him round.
VOE0503 ...Fifty thousand?
VOE0504 Pleasure doing business. Do your best with him. Or don't. I'll know.
VOE0505 He already told you no. That's the only answer you're getting from either of us.
VOE0506 Shame. Open systems get copied, you know.
VOE0507 Yeah. That's the point, genius.
VOE0601 ~y~SFTV NEWS:~w~ An independent San Fierro lab demonstrated a sound experiment live at the pier, while schools and a radio club across the city reproduced it at the same time.
VOE0602 ~y~SFTV NEWS:~w~ The lab's code and data are freely available on an open registry. A venture firm's offer to license the work was declined.
VOE0603 Forty thousand downloads. Three replications. Two of them by people under eighteen.
VOE0604 So what now? More experiments?
VOE0605 Always. The lab's open whenever you want it, Carl. R.A.I.N. has questions nobody's asked yet.
VOE0606 Long as none of them gets the cops on me.
VOE0607 I can't promise that. But I can promise we'll check the evidence first.
